
FWNX
=======================

Framework for a New eXecution environment

FWNX is an experimental kernel project focused on building a kernel
with its own architecture, system interfaces, memory management, and
hardware support.

About
--------------------

FWNX is a kernel development project intended for experimentation
with low-level systems programming and operating system development.

Goals
--------------------

- Develop a kernel from scratch.
- Implement kernel initialization and basic console output.
- Add physical and virtual memory management.
- Implement interrupt and exception handling.
- Develop device drivers.
- Implement system calls.
- Add process and thread management.
- Explore filesystem support.

Project Structure
--------------------

The source tree will evolve as kernel development progresses.

Building
--------------------

Build instructions will be added once the initial build system
and boot process have been implemented.

Status
--------------------

FWNX is in early development.

